WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.411
Graduation is a ship checklist, not a binge certificate.

00:00:03.411 --> 00:00:06.064
This lesson is about capstone: ship checklist.

00:00:06.064 --> 00:00:06.822
Graduation criteria.

00:00:06.822 --> 00:00:09.475
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:09.475 --> 00:00:13.265
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:13.265 --> 00:00:18.950
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:23.119
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:23.119 --> 00:00:27.288
Stay practical: complete ship checklist before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:27.608 --> 00:00:32.435
Complete: problem, buyer, offer, price, page, talks, close, delivery, testimonial, week system.

00:00:32.435 --> 00:00:34.848
Remember the objective: complete ship checklist.

00:00:34.848 --> 00:00:39.273
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:39.273 --> 00:00:44.100
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:48.524
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:48.524 --> 00:00:53.351
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:53.351 --> 00:00:56.167
Talk to a real person when possible.

00:00:56.167 --> 00:00:57.776
Feedback beats guessing alone.

00:00:58.096 --> 00:00:59.600
Any gap is homework.

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:01.103
Do not fake done.

